      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
